          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Machine Learning",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Excited by Big Data, Machine Learning and Predictive Software? Interested in creating new state-of-the-art solutions using Machine Learning and Data Mining techniques on Terabytes of Data?",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "At Amazon, we are developing state-of-the-art large-scale Machine Learning Services and Applications on the Cloud involving Terabytes of data. We work on applying predictive technology to a wide spectrum of problems in areas such as Amazon Retail, Seller Services, Customer Service, Alexa, Chatbots and so on. We are looking for talented and experienced Machine Learning Scientists (Masters/Ph.D. in a related area preferred) who can apply innovative Machine Learning techniques to real-world e-Commerce problems. You will get to work in a team dedicated to advancing Machine Learning technology at Amazon and converting it to business-impacting solutions.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Major responsibilities",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Use machine learning, data mining and statistical techniques to create new, scalable solutions for business problems",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Analyze and extract relevant information from large amounts of Amazons historical business data to help automate and optimize key processes",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Design, develop and evaluate highly innovative models for predictive learning",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Establish scalable, efficient, automated processes for large scale data analyses model development, model validation and model implementation",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Research and implement novel machine learning and statistical approaches",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Basic Qualifications",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- A Masters and/or PhD in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Operational research, Statistics or in a highly quantitative field",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Experience in predictive modelling and analysis, predictive software development",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Strong problem-solving ability",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Good skills with Java/Scala or C++, Perl/Python (or similar scripting language)",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Experience in using R, Matlab, or any other statistical software",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Strong communication and data presentation skills",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Preferred Qualifications",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Experience handling gigabyte and terabyte size datasets",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Experience working with distributed systems and grid computing",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Knowledge of the latest and state of the art ML technology",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "- Publications or presentation in recognized Machine Learning and Data Mining journals/conferences",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Software Engineer",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "As a member of our Software Engineering Group you will dive head-first into creating innovative solutions that advance businesses and careers. You'll join an inspiring and curious team of technologists dedicated to improving the design, analytics, development, coding, testing and application programming that goes into creating high quality software and new products. You'll be tasked with keeping the team and other key stakeholders up to speed on the progress of what's being developed. Coming in with an understanding of the importance of end-to-end software development-such as Agile frameworks-is key. And best of all, you'll be working with and sharing ideas, information and innovation with our global team of technologists from all over the world. JPMorgan Chase & Co. is an equal opportunity employer and affirmative action employer Disability/Veteran",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "This role requires a wide variety of strengths and capabilities, including:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Advanced knowledge of application, data and infrastructure architecture disciplines",
