          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "DevOps Engineer",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Turvo India is the world class R&D arm of the California-based software company, Turvo Inc. Turvo is the only real-time collaborative logistics platform that connects anyone, anywhere to move things. Our platform creates a smarter way for shippers, brokers, and carriers to seamlessly work together to get things done faster. We are re-imagining how the world moves things!",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "At Turvo we always like to push the boundaries of technologies and work on solving problems that have not been solved. We are agile startup-minded engineers and our culture emphasises on the policy of learn and teach as we care about building an environment where there is a constant flow of knowledge without the classroom learning techniques. As an early-stage employee, you will be uniquely positioned to learn a lot while solving complex problems and writing software both impactful to our customers and critical to our company’s success. Our team sizes are small to encourage impactful contributions from each engineer and to promote meaningful collaboration. We offer competitive salaries and a range of benefits. Moreover, we will give you the chance to work with other awesome engineers and product designers.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "The primary role entails",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "➢ Managing all infrastructure as code by defining desired state",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "➢ Crafting continuous integration and continuous deployment pipelines",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "➢ Standardising, automating and documenting all things.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "➢ Improving our build and release tooling and processes.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "➢ Defining best practices for virtualisation, configuration managements, source control, continuous integration, continuous delivery, automated testing and release management",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "➢ Building tools for internal use to support software engineering best practices.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "➢ Bringing new automation technologies to improve the velocity and quality of our engineering efforts",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
