          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "In a constantly changing world, we work together with our people, clients and communities to enable them to fulfill their potential to do great things. We believe that by bringing everyone together, we can solve problems using innovative technology that can create a world that is sustainable and secure. At NTT, we encourage you to remain continuously curious, as that is what keeps you fast, flexible and relevant. No two days will be the same but that is what will help you grow and realize your full potential.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "The power is in your hands to do great things. It’s time to lead the change, be the authentic you, to solve difficult challenges, to set the pace of change and to unleash your potential.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Want to be a part of our team?",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "The MS Engineer (L1) is responsible for providing a managed service to clients to ensure that their IT infrastructure and systems remain operational through proactively identifying, investigating and resolving technical incidents and problems and to restore service to clients by managing incidents to resolution. Their primary objective is to ensure zero missed service level agreement conditions. The MS Engineer (L1) focuses on first line support for standard and low complexity incidents and service requests.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Radford reference:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "\"Performs IT functions such as design, analysis, evaluation, testing, debugging and implementation of applications programs supporting the company infrastructure business processes and operations and/or network-based (cloud) product systems. Analyzes, installs, acquires, modifies and supports operating systems, database or utilities software. Plans, conducts and directs the analysis of business problems with automated systems solutions. Analyzes, designs, acquires and implements projects for LAN and/or WAN systems. Plans, designs, acquires and implements telecommunications voice/wire systems. At higher job levels, may contribute to the development, testing, evaluation or design of system or infrastructure architecture used throughout the IT solution set.\"",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Working at NTT",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Key Roles and Responsibilities:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Monitors client infrastructure and solutions",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Identify problems and errors prior to or when they occur",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Routinely identify common incidents and opportunities for avoidance as well as general opportunities for incident reduction",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Investigate first line incidents assigned and identify the root cause of incidents and problems",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Fulfil approved requests following agreed procedures",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
