            "utterance": "Description",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "The role involves building and maintaining strong partnerships with key business leaders in order to successfully lead business initiatives. Additionally it is meaningful to build a collaboration with other IT teams effectively to drive alignment and efficiency on joint methodologies, architectures, co-development frameworks, etc. Driving alignment and initiatives across the worldwide and regional development teams to achieve global goals - such as common frameworks, production support model, retirement of legacy solutions, etc. is vital to this role. Leading Project Managers, Business Analysts and technical teams to define and build rapid internal solutions that enable key processes within the Operations function is mandatory. Additionally, managing a team of developers, providing technical leadership, governance - focus on stabilizing agility, flexibility, supportability, scale and consistency is required.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Education & Experience",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Bachelor’s degree is required, preferably in Computer Science, CIS/MIS, or related discipline with an information technology focus. MBA / MS preferred; focus on Operations management/supply chain management is a plus.",
