            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Software Engineer",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "As a member of our Software Engineering Group, we look first and foremost for people who are passionate around solving business problems through innovation and engineering practices. You'll be required to apply your depth of knowledge and expertise to all aspects of the software development lifecycle, as well as partner continuously with your many stakeholders on a daily basis to stay focused on common goals. We embrace a culture of experimentation and constantly strive for improvement and learning. You'll work in a collaborative, trusting, thought-provoking environment-one that encourages diversity of thought and creative solutions that are in the best interests of our customers globally.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "This role requires a wide variety of strengths and capabilities, including:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "BS/BA degree or equivalent experience",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Advanced knowledge of application, data, and infrastructure architecture disciplines",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Understanding of architecture and design across all systems",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Working proficiency in developmental toolsets",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Knowledge of industry-wide technology trends and best practices",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Ability to work in large, collaborative teams to achieve organizational goals",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Passionate about building an innovative culture",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Proficiency in one or more modern programming languages",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Understanding of software skills such as business analysis, development, maintenance, and software improvement",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Bachelor's degree in engineering or Degree from reputed organization 2. 5+ years of Industry experience, preferably in IT industry. 3. Knowledge of Java/Spring, SQL (Sybase/Oracle), Any caching application, React 4. Strong communication skills, both written and verbal 5.Ability to work collaboratively in teams and develop meaningful relationships to achieve common goals",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "JPMorgan Chase & Co. is an equal opportunity employer and affirmative action employer Disability/VeteranJPMorgan Chase & Co., one of the oldest financial institutions, offers innovative financial solutions to millions of consumers, small businesses and many of the world's most prominent corporate, institutional and government clients under the J.P. Morgan and Chase brands. Our history spans over 200 years and today we are a leader in investment banking, consumer and small business banking, commercial banking, financial transaction processing and asset management.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. In accordance with applicable law, we make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as any mental health or physical disability needs.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Machine Learning",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Qualcomm India Private Limited",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Engineering Group, Engineering Group > Machine Learning Engineering",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Job Overview:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Qualcomm is a company of inventors that unlocked 5G ushering in an age of rapid acceleration in connectivity and new possibilities that will transform industries, create jobs, and enrich lives. But this is just the beginning. It takes inventive minds with diverse skills, backgrounds, and cultures to transform 5Gs potential into world-changing technologies and products. This is the Invention Age - and this is where you come in.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Join a dynamic team at Qualcomm focused on advancing state-of-the-art in Machine Learning applications. The team invents Machine Learning techniques that will change the way chips are designed, by reducing long-loop iterations and enabling deeper exploration of the chip design solution space. The candidate will be expected to work on identifying new opportunities to apply Machine Learning in chip design, exploring advanced ML solution techniques, developing/testing/tuning ML algorithms, and writing/deploying/supporting production-ready software to chip design teams.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Minimum Qualifications",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "An amazing team player most important!",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Expertise in Machine Learning theory and hands-on programming is a must",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Experience with advanced ML techniques (e.g., CNN, GNN, RNN, RL)",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Strong analytical and communication skills",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Familiarity with VLSI is a strong plus",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "B. Tech, M. Tech or Ph.D. in CS/ECE, with 3-10 years experience after Bachelors degree",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Applicants: If you need an accommodation, during the application/hiring process, you may request an accommodation by sending email to accommodationsupport",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "To all Staffing and Recruiting Agencies: Our Careers Site is only for individuals seeking a job at Qualcomm. Staffing and recruiting agencies and individuals being represented by an agency are not authorized to use this site or to submit profiles, applications or resumes, and any such submissions will be considered unsolicited. Qualcomm does not accept unsolicited resumes or applications from agencies. Please do not forward resumes to our jobs alias, Qualcomm employees or any other company location. Qualcomm is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes/applications.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Java Developer",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Responsible to perform software development for internal web-based and other ES3 software projects, US Air Force projects and in support of ES3 engineering projects in a team-oriented work environment. Demonstrate ability to use software development best practices in activities such as requirements analysis, design, coding, software configuration management, documentation and testing. Must have the ability to effectively work independently and within a team. Must be able to problem solve and be self-motivated. Must be able to interact with management, engineers, subcontractors, team members and customers in a professional and collaborative manner.",
            "intent": "job_description"
