          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "DevOps Engineer",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Who we Are:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "DevX is the central tooling organization in the Core Software Group (CSG), responsible for the various SW development and test tools; customized for Cisco's engineering requirements and used in the developer's workflow. The core objective of the group is to improve engineering efficiency and provide better user experience by modernizing the tools used by Cisco's dev and test community",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Who you Are:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "You are a passionate engineer having excellent grasp of OS concepts & compilers with a hands-on experience working in an Build tools environment. You are passionate about developing quality software. You are eager & keep yourself updated on the standard methodologies, tools & technologies in the industry. You enjoy working in a team environment & demonstrate a strong can-do attitude.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Shown experience in Build tools like Make or GMake",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Hands on experience on sophisticated debugging and problem-solving skills",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Expertise in either Python or C++ with Unix/Linux",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Expertise in CI tools like Jenkins with prior experience in setting up CI/CD pipelines",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Strong understanding of the compilation aspects with ability to work independently",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Experience in enterprise embedded systems",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Excellent verbal & written communication skills",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Your responsibilities include:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Design and develop new software product features.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Give innovative ideas for multiple module architecture.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Define product internal/external interfaces.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Develop sophisticated, multiple modules of code independently.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Write complete functional and design specs independently.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Talk to other functional groups, evaluate and recommend tools",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "What You’ll Do:",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "You will be a part of a central team developing in-house solution for capturing real-time code coverage metrics on an embedded system. You will develop and sustain the solution across multiple product lines, various compiler flavors and OS’s; continuously exploring opportunity to further improve the solution with new functionality, approaches, or incorporating the latest developments.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "#WeAreCisco, where each person is outstanding, but we bring our talents to work as a team and make a difference powering an inclusive future for all.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "We accept digital, and help our customers implement change in their digital businesses. Some may think we’re “old” (36 years strong) and only about hardware, but we’re also a software company. And a security company. We even invented an intuitive network that adapts, predicts, learns and protects. No other company can do what we do – you can’t put us in a box!",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "But “Digital Transformation” is an empty buzz phrase without a culture that allows for innovation, creativity, and yes, even failure (if you learn from it.)",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Day to day, we focus on the give and take. We give our best, give our egos a break, and give of ourselves (because giving back is built into our DNA.) We take accountability, bold steps, and take difference to heart. Because without diversity of thought and a dedication to equality for all, there is no moving forward.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "So, you have colorful hair? Don’t care. Tattoos? Show off your ink. Like polka dots? That’s cool. Pop culture geek? Many of us are. Passion for technology and world changing? Be you, with us!",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Machine Learning",
            "intent": "job_title"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Who we are: Fueled by a fundamental belief that having access to financial services creates opportunity, PayPal (NASDAQ: PYPL) is committed to democratizing financial services and empowering people and businesses to join and thrive in the global economy. Our open digital payments platform gives PayPal’s 286 million active account holders the confidence to connect and transact in new and powerful ways, whether they are online, on a mobile device, in an app, or in person. Through a combination of technological innovation and strategic partnerships, PayPal creates better ways to manage and move money, and offers choice and flexibility when sending payments, paying or getting paid. Available in more than 200 markets around the world, the PayPal platform, including Braintree, Venmo and Xoom enables consumers and merchants to receive money in more than 100 currencies, withdraw funds in 56 currencies and hold balances in their PayPal accounts in 25 currencies.",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
            "domain": "default",
            "utterance": "Job Description Summary: The candidate will be part of PayPal Privacy Engineering Team. The candidate will be responsible for analysis, design, coding and building web platforms. The individual should be self-motivated, team-oriented problem solver, possess creative problem-solving skills .",
            "intent": "job_description"
          },
          {
