        "en",
        "About the company:"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Company Name: Hansel Pvt. Ltd."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Location: - Bangalore"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Team Strength: 30+ People"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "About the Company: We are a fast growing startup in the product optimization space working out of our Bangalore office. Because of the innovative technology that we’re developing, we’ve seen rapid adoption in the last couple of years and are now working with some of the largest Indian companies. You can find out more details about the product and company over here."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "The core team comprises of folks from IIT-IIIT-IIM with experience in building products that cater to millions of users a day, for companies like Flipkart, Zynga, and Disney."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Hansel has been recognized as a Gartner cool vendor within 2 years of launch. Gartner cool vendors are companies offering a technology that is innovative, impactful and intriguing."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Hansel has also been awarded as one of the top 10 most innovative technology companies from India by Nasscom in 2016. We were one of the top Tech30 companies of Techsparks 2016."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "What will you be doing?"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "We’re working on a technology that allows product managers to create powerful contexts from data points (data ingested from various sources such as analytics systems, microservices backends, applications etc) and trigger actions relevant to those contexts, all from a visual drag and drop interface minimizing the need to involve engineering teams. Hansel bridges the gap between business and engineering teams to enable companies to operate and iterate on their products faster than ever before. Onboarding each customer would mean signing up for millions of their end users. You’ll be responsible for the development of Hansel’s scalable backend and handling terabytes of data streams. You would also be instrumental in helping shape the product and defining its scope."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "DevOps Engineer"
      ],
      [
