      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Texas A&M University is committed to enriching the learning and working environment for all visitors, students, faculty, and staff by promoting a culture that embraces inclusion, diversity, equity, and accountability. Diverse perspectives, talents and identities are vital to accomplishing our mission and living our core values ."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Texas A&M University’s Enterprise Information Systems (EIS) department provides reliable and cost-effective, mission-critical, enterprise-wide information to the Texas A&M University’s main campus (including School of Law, Health Science Center, and other locations across Texas) and its branch campuses in Galveston and Qatar to support the academic, administrative, research and recruiting missions of Texas A&M University. EIS systems allow students to apply, enroll, pay and graduate, then transition from Texas A&M University to careers. The EIS team manages the information in the Compass system, a software product called Banner, which assists academic services to ensure effective and efficient processes, accurate and timely reporting, and quality services for students, faculty and staff."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "What we want"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Enterprise Information Systems is seeking a Software Application Developer I who will be responsible for performing routine software development support functions, under direction. Time management, resourcefulness, organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work as a motivated self-starter are crucial talents and skills for success in this position. We need a highly productive individual who subscribes to and supports our commitment to Inclusion, Diversity, Equity and Accountability (IDEA) as stated above. This this description appeals to you, then apply for this great opportunity."
      ],
