        "Software Engineer"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Neustar is an information services and technology company and a leader in identity resolution providing the data and technology that enables trusted connections between companies and people at the moments that matter most. More information is available at https://www.home.neustar."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Job Requisition:"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "R-3236 Software Engineer II - MII (Open)"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Primary Location:"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Job Description:"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Who are we?"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "As a company built on the foundation of Privacy by Design, for more than 20 years Neustar’s unique capabilities have made us the leader in the field of responsible identity resolution. Neustar enables trusted connections between companies and people at the moments that matter the most, with world-class and industry leading solutions in Marketing, Risk, Communications, Security and Registry services."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "The Software Engineer II - MII is a key partner in bringing technical expertise to ensure the quality and accuracy of the Neustar product suite. These product suites enable the data processing and analytics necessary to help people, businesses, and organizations make better decisions. The engineer filling this role will be responsible for helping customers in the areas of data acquisition, data infrastructure and data analytics. The role is based out of India at the Neustar's offices in Bangalore."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "This is a full-stack developer position -- own the end to end design and development effort of features for the dashboard for our products with a focus on data rich interactions."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "This also includes building out the back-end REST services."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Deconstruct challenging data interaction problems, adapt a lot of analytical moving parts, use cases, and construct one whole, continuous and intuitive UX that engage, and delight our clients."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Support the business process reengineering of current processes and help streamline and refine the processes"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Work with product owners and external partners when external partner integrations are not functioning as expected. Enable metrics to track these external integrations and alert when there are issues with these integrations."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Qualifications/Education"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "5 - 8 years’ experience in software engineering"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Bachelor’s degree in computer science or engineering discipline"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Strong coding and debugging skills with experience in web technologies including one or more of the following: Java, Hibernate, Spring boot, Javascript (React, Angular, Node, D3 etc.), AJAX, CSS"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Adept at service-oriented architecture, design and development with hands on experience developing Java REST services"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Worked with authentication technologies like SAML, OAuth, SSL etc."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Hands on experience with one or more web and application server technologies such as Apache Tomcat, Nginx, Jersey server, OSGi and other relevant frameworks"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Hands on experience with continuous integration and continuous deployment tools including Chef, Jenkins"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Hands on experience with code control and code review tools like Git, Gerrit"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Good exposure to databases, SQL queries"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Fast executor with a track record of delivering complex projects on time; responds under pressures of time and uncertainty"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Strong written, editing, proofreading and oral communication"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Strong inter-personal communication and collaboration skills. The candidate must be able to work independently & must possess strong communication skills."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "A good team player, high level of personal commitment & 'can do' attitude."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Strong communication skill to communicate at all levels, which includes interaction within the team & with senior management."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "The candidate should have proactive approach towards problem solving."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Good analysis skills in order to troubleshoot and resolve the problems"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "At Neustar, we are committed to the growth and development of our employees whose individual skills, curiosity and passion for their work, contribute to the overall success of our business. Our core values (Accountability, Collaboration, Transparency, Resilience, and Respect) are the driving force of our culture across our locations around the globe. We offer our employees a comprehensive benefits package including perks such as tuition reimbursement, awesome company discounts, back-up day care, community service events, pet and baby swag and much more! We are all learning and creating together; and having some major fun along the way."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "JOIN US! We can’t wait to meet you!"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Neustar does not accept unsolicited resumes from external firms or agencies. Neustar will not be responsible for placement fees associated with unsolicited resumes."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Diversity, inclusion and teamwork are second nature to Neustar; and these values permeate our entire business structure. Neustar is committed to creating an environment where a wide spectrum of opinions and beliefs are actively sought, listened to and respected. Further, our talented workforce draws from the many geographic areas and markets in which Neustar operates worldwide, which represents a distinct competitive advantage. The rich and varied personal and professional backgrounds of our employees make Neustar a dynamic and rewarding company at which to build a career. We invite you to join us."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "EOE of Minorities/Females/Vets/Disability"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Neustar, Inc. considers all applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, or status as a Vietnam-era or special disabled veteran in accordance with federal law and other state and local requirements. Neustar, Inc., complies with applicable state and local laws prohibiting discrimination in employment and provides reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities in accordance with the American with Disabilities Act (ADA) and applicable state and local laws."
      ],
