        "en",
        "Introduction"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "As an Application Developer, you will lead IBM into the future by translating system requirements into the design and development of customized systems in an agile environment. The success of IBM is in your hands as you transform vital business needs into code and drive innovation. Your work will power IBM and its clients globally, collaborating and integrating code into enterprise systems. You will have access to the latest education, tools and technology, and a limitless career path with the world’s technology leader. Come to IBM and make a global impact!"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Your Role and Responsibilities"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "For this position, we need professionals with the following experiences: - Professional capable of receiving a development demand and delivering it from start to finish, in front of products related to software development. Have the ability to develop a solution from requirements and data modeling, through data structuring, architecture and implementation, to communication with servers, databases and internal and external services. Experience with agile methodologies, preferably Scrum; - Understanding different types of software requirements; - Knowledge in object-oriented programming; - Knowledge in software architecture; Knowledge about application server; - Knowledge in relational and non-relational databases."
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "Required Technical and Professional Expertise"
      ],
      [
        "en",
        "For this position, we need professionals with the following experiences: - Professional capable of receiving a development demand and delivering it from start to finish, in front of products related to software development. Have the ability to develop a solution from requirements and data modeling, through data structuring, architecture and implementation, to communication with servers, databases and internal and external services. Experience with agile methodologies, preferably Scrum; - Understanding different types of software requirements; - Knowledge in object-oriented programming; - Knowledge in software architecture; Knowledge about application server; - Knowledge in relational and non-relational databases."
